  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Editorial Efímera begins with our encounter with an archive of 193 slides in a trash can in Santiago, on June 6th, 2018 at 6:40 pm. This set of images dramatically discarded in a public space lost their private quality, along with the fragmentation of the narratives that held them together as a unit. On the other hand, our encounter with them set in motion a process of appropriation and assimilation, which concludes in a number of actions whose only aim is to exhibit this archive by displaying its parts, dispensing a last moment of existence before the total dissolution of the image and the irrevocable extinction of its narration. For that purpose, we have created an Editorial Efímera, in charge of performing 193 actions -- one for each image -- to forge the dissolution rite of each one of the components of this archive. Completion will determine the end of the publishing house itself... The 193 images contained in the photographic archive which gave birth to Editorial Efímera are collected in this artist's book -- with one detail: none of the images can reall be seen, but only the slide's contour and the inscription where the photograph was taken"</subfield>
  </datafield>
